  [exit 2]
== help screens
> env COLUMNS
> parser prog=backup-tool usage=usage: %prog [options] SRC DEST version=%prog 2.4.1 description=%prog copies a source tree to a destination, keeping a rotating set of dated snapshots and pruning the oldest ones once the set is full. epilog=Exit status is 0 on success and 2 on a usage error. Report bugs to the operations team.
> option -v,--verbose action=count help=print more detail; repeat for even more
  -v/--verbose: action=count type=None dest=verbose nargs=None
> option -n,--dry-run action=store_true help=show what would be copied, but copy nothing
  -n/--dry-run: action=store_true type=None dest=dry_run nargs=None
> option --keep type=int default=i:7 metavar=N help=keep N snapshots [default: %default]
  --keep: action=store type=int dest=keep nargs=1
> option --compress choices=l:none,gzip,zstd default=s:zstd help=compression (%default by default; none, gzip or zstd)
  --compress: action=store type=choice dest=compress nargs=1
> option --secret-debug action=store_true help=@SUPPRESS
  --secret-debug: action=store_true type=None dest=secret_debug nargs=None
> group Filtering These options decide which files are copied. They are applied in the order given.
> option -x,--exclude action=append metavar=GLOB help=skip files that match GLOB
  -x/--exclude: action=append type=string dest=exclude nargs=1
> option --max-size-in-bytes-per-file type=int metavar=BYTES help=skip larger files
  --max-size-in-bytes-per-file: action=store type=int dest=max_size_in_bytes_per_file nargs=1
> option --since help=only files changed since %default default=n:
  --since: action=store type=string dest=since nargs=1
> endgroup
> group Expert
> option --io-threads type=int default=s:4
  --io-threads: action=store type=int dest=io_threads nargs=1
> endgroup
> help
  | Usage: backup-tool [options] SRC DEST
  |
  | backup-tool copies a source tree to a destination, keeping a rotating set of
  | dated snapshots and pruning the oldest ones once the set is full.
  |
  | Options:
  |   --version             show program's version number and exit
  |   -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  |   -v, --verbose         print more detail; repeat for even more
  |   -n, --dry-run         show what would be copied, but copy nothing
  |   --keep=N              keep N snapshots [default: 7]
  |   --compress=COMPRESS   compression (zstd by default; none, gzip or zstd)
  |
  |   Filtering:
  |     These options decide which files are copied. They are applied in the
  |     order given.
  |
  |     -x GLOB, --exclude=GLOB
  |                         skip files that match GLOB
  |     --max-size-in-bytes-per-file=BYTES
  |                         skip larger files
  |     --since=SINCE       only files changed since none
  |
  |   Expert:
  |     --io-threads=IO_THREADS
  |
  | Exit status is 0 on success and 2 on a usage error. Report bugs to the
  | operations team.
